"text": "The gates are: - escher-telemetry's and escher-driver's unit tests; - the error-text target in both layout modes, package-alone (its engine branch reading no engine item); - the same target with the engine's `tracing` compiled (`--features dioxus-native-dom/tracing`, as the previous chunk   read it), so the engine item and the sink's engine line are read locally as the workspace leg reads them in CI   (test-plan · decision/per-package-green-not-workspace-green); - the companions the diff moves:   - `stand_mcp_tools` and seven_guis' `mcp_server` and `cli_commands`: `caused`'s help is served by `help` and as     the acting tools' descriptions, the same bytes on both surfaces;   - `stand_act_errors`, `stand_replay` and `stand_act_spans`;   - escher-telemetry's process checks `telemetry_scrub`, `telemetry_drop` and `telemetry_panic_hook`, and seven_guis'     `host_log` and `mcp_log`, which show that the sink prints what it printed; - a probe that the help no longer lists `error` among the hidden names; - then the pre-push gate and `stand-repeat`."
},
{
"from": 133,
"to": 135,
"text": "No boot-path touchpoint changes a binary's start. `host_log` and `mcp_log` drive both binaries' roles, and stand in for the smoke. There is no live leg. The coverage leg is not listed: escher-driver's change is help and doc text, and the capture code is escher-telemetry's, which has no floor."
},
{
"from": 137,
"to": 146,
"text": "Each new check is controlled red-before-green (tests S2). After the steps are green, /implement runs three one-shot `gate.py control` runs, never entries: - **`error` back in the answer's set** (`capture.rs`, the private constant gains `\"error\"`). Fired on the   escher-telemetry unit entry, case: the table test of step 2. Fired again on the error-text entry, case: the test   that runs `every_failure`, `each_failure_answers_what_failed_where_and_from_which_source`. - **`error` out of the sink's set** (`format.rs`, `\"error\",` removed from `CONTENT_FIELDS`). Fired on the   escher-telemetry unit entry, case: `content_fields_redact_for_any_target`. Its removal also opens `error` in the   answer's set only if step 1 derived one set from the other, which step 1 forbids. - **The capture judging by the sink's set again** (`capture.rs:276` restored to `CONTENT_FIELDS`). Fired on the   tracing error-text entry, case: step 6's engine test."
},
{
"from": 148,
"to": 148,
"text": "Each control names the edit's text and the case by its test name (gate-contract.md §Control)."
},
{
"from": 150,
"to": 153,
"text": "The diff is not OS-sensitive: no `cfg` site is added or changed, and the texts compared are a parse error's Display and fixed strings. An acceptance reads CI, because the workspace test leg on linux, windows and macOS is where the engine branch runs on every OS, and the socket case is unix-gated. So the operator's hygiene, push and CI entries stand."
}
],
